From da74deff3575cc33b5f8eabe2dd7808f3e1c34ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rust-mos-sync <rust-mos-sync@localhost>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:22:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rust_target: add every remaining llvm-mos-sdk platform as a
 MOS target

32 more built-in mos-<platform>-none targets (docs/backlog.md item 1),
covering every mos-<platform>-clang driver in llvm-mos-sdk's README
(Apple II, Atari 2600/5200/8-bit variants, Atari Lynx, Ben Eater's
breadboard, Commander X16, Commodore 128/PET/VIC-20, CP/M-65, Dodo,
GEOS, MEGA65, every NES mapper + FDS, Ohio Scientific, Neo6502,
RP6502, PC Engine (+CD), RPC/8e, Watara Supervision).

base::mos::target() now takes an explicit cpu, since a few platforms
widen the ISA beyond plain mos6502 (mosw65c02/mos65c02/mos45gs02/
moshuc6280/mos65el02) or restrict it to undocumented opcodes only
(mos6502x, Atari 2600) - matched to each platform's own clang.cfg
default (inherited from its SDK PARENT platform when it sets none
itself), not the CMake-internal flags some platforms use to build
their own C library. build-rust.sh and test.sh's std tier discover
mos-* targets generically, so all 32 get built and core/alloc-tested
without further script changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HQ3NU61e5cSU6oYFJ1J76p
